PCB Layout — Plant Monitor

This folder is intended for the KiCad PCB layout files for the Plant Monitor.

Goal

The goal is to turn the circuit schematic into a custom PCB that connects the ESP32, sensors, OLED display, and status LEDs.

Planned PCB Design Steps
Import the finalized schematic into the PCB Editor.
Update the PCB from the schematic.
Define the board outline.
Arrange components and connectors.
Set the design rules and track widths.
Route the electrical connections.
Add a ground plane if appropriate.
Run the Design Rules Checker (DRC).
Review the board before manufacturing.
Planned Layout Considerations
Keep sensor and display connections accessible.
Place connectors so external modules can be connected easily.
Keep power and ground routing reliable.
Ensure the selected footprints match the actual components.
Provide suitable mounting and USB access for the chosen ESP32 development-board arrangement.
Files

The following file will be added when PCB layout begins:

PlantMonitor.kicad_pcb — KiCad PCB layout
